SQUARK_FEX_ABI_FLAGS: flags are dead across calls and returns in listed modules

The dead flag pass treats every exit from a multiblock as reading all flags, so before each call and
return the JIT keeps AF and PF, the canonical carry (cfinv) and the flags of the epilogue's add to rsp.
The x64 calling convention leaves flags undefined across a call and a return, and compiled code never
passes a value in them; hand-written or protected code can, so this is opt in per module.

SQUARK_FEX_ABI_FLAGS lists pieces of module paths (';'-separated, any case). The ARM64EC frontend keeps
the address ranges of matching images (append only, cleared when unmapped) and sets
FEXCore::Context::SqABILocalFlagsFn; the dead flag pass then takes no flags as read at an ExitFunction
with the Call or Return hint for a block whose entry is in such a range. Without the variable nothing
changes. Microsoft Flight Simulator's WebAssembly modules (WASM\MSFS2024\<package>\*.dll, compiled by
LLVM) are such code; the game's own executable is protected and must not be listed.

FBW A380X benchmark with SQUARK_FEX_ABI_FLAGS=fbwbench.exe: 2.729M -> 2.630M instructions (-3.6%),
488k -> 485k cycles per tick, median tick 0.1105 -> 0.1095 ms.
